  "summary_en": "UK statutory instrument implementing the EC Machinery Directive 89/392/EEC. It prohibits supplying machinery unless it meets essential health and safety requirements, has gone through conformity assessment and carries the CE mark, and it sets offences and penalties. Robots are mentioned only in passing. Later amended, then revoked and replaced by the 2008 Regulations.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No person may supply relevant machinery unless it meets the essential health and safety requirements, is in fact safe, and has an EC declaration of conformity and CE marking",
   "Responsible persons must compile technical files; Schedule 4 high-hazard machinery requires approved-body involvement or EC type-examination",
   "The Secretary of State appoints UK approved bodies for conformity assessment",
   "Essential requirements cover control system safety and reliability, emergency stops, guards, and instructions, including controls for robot training",
   "Breaches are criminal offences, with a due diligence defence and liability for company officers"
  ],
